-Any other `##` heading is prose, except one that reads like a change: a heading whose first word, in any case and with any trailing `:`, `;`, `,`, `.` or `-` ignored, is add, adds, added, adding, set, sets, setting, replace, replaces, replaced or replacing, or whose second word is `at` in any case, fails as a malformed change heading unless it is one of the four forms above, so a prose heading such as "Setting up the host" or "Look at the target" is renamed. A file sets each point, and replaces each module, at most once. A `##` line inside a fenced code block (opened by three or more backticks or tildes) is not a heading and changes nothing.
+Any other `##` heading is prose, except one that reads like a change: a heading whose first word, in any case and with any trailing `:`, `;`, `,`, `.` or `-` ignored, is add, adds, added, adding, set, sets, setting, replace, replaces, replaced or replacing, or whose second word is `at` in any case, fails as a malformed change heading unless it is one of the four forms above, so a prose heading such as "Setting up the host" or "Look at the target" is renamed. A file sets each point, and replaces each module, at most once. A section runs from its heading to the next `##` heading, prose or change, so a replacement gives its own structure `###` headings and deeper. A `##` line inside a fenced code block is not a heading and changes nothing: a fence opens with a run of three or more backticks or tildes indented at most three spaces, a backtick run whose info string holds a backtick opening none, and closes with a run of the same character at least as long, indented at most three spaces and followed only by spaces or tabs; a fence still open at the end of the file fails. The check also fails a `## Set at` section with no non-blank line, anything under `types/` or `traits/` that is not a conditional workflow at its key's path (a README there included), and a folder under `types/` that is no product type.
 
